To the Public,                                       September 9, 1992

I am distributing "Daymare I" as Shareware. This game also appeared on the
Atari ST as "Daymare". The 2 player version for the Atari ST was known as
"Mystic Mirror".

If you can afford it, I strongly hope that you will register your game with
me. For $16 you will receive the latest version of the program, a bonus
program, and you will be on my mailing list for all future products and
newsletters. Your support helps me to continue writing and improving
my games.

I am currently working on "Daymare 3". This game is being designed from
scratch to work on the IBM as a one player game. I will be using VGA
graphics for a 320 by 200 pixel screen in 256 colors. I am using flight
simulator type graphics for a more realistic dungeon like that in Ultima
Underworld(TM). It will also incorporate sound and scanned art.

MAKE A BACKUP OF THIS DISK FOR YOUR ARCHIVES.

OPERATING INSTRUCTIONS
     A PC with at least a 286 processor is recommended to run "Daymare I".
     Files included are GAME.EXE,RQFRAMES.DAT,RQICONS.DAT,RQMAPS.DAT.
     To start a game double click GAME.EXE and follow the screen
instructions.
     To quit a game in progress press <escape> and the game will exit
immediately.  You  should save your game if  you  want  it before
you exit as a save is not made during exiting.
     To save a game click on the disk icon with your mouse. The game
will be saved as "PLAYER.SAV".
     To attack a creature, click on the sword Icon. A slash mark will
appear on the screen when you attack. The weapon in your right hand
is the weapon used to attack with. If you do not have a weapon in that
hand then bare-handed combat is used.
     To use the special magic of an item (if any) then select on the
white diamond. Note some items are one-shot. There are no multi-use
items.
     To cast a spell, you must select some spell symbols, then click
on the white diamond. If you select to the left or right of the diamond
then you can erase all the selected symbols. Note that you cannot use
the special power of items while a spell is currently ready to be cast.
A miscast spell drains all your stamina. So does a spell that is to
difficult for you to cast. If you see the spell in a book and you can't
seem to cast it, then try again when you gain a level.
     There are four different kinds of armor. They are in the order that
they appear: Physical, Fire, Electrical, and Poison. Note that clothing
will give certain protection in each of the categories. Poison includes
death spells and chemical attacks such as venomous clouds. If you are
hit for damage, then an "X" will appear in each corner. A gold "X" is
a magical attack. Physical armor protects against this randomly. A luck
spell will cut all damage (after armor) in half. A bless spell causes
a successful attack to only do one point of damage (ending the spell).
     Note that some things have weight. The higher your weight in stuff
being carried, the slower your stamina is restored. Stamina is used up
when casting spells or attacking. If your stamina is to low then you
will be unable to attack or cast spells or use some items.
     The strike row will be occasionally be followed by a number. This
number is the total damage done to critters at that instant. This helps
you to determine if an attack form is having any effect.
     Strength has effect on damage done with weapon attacks. It also
allows faster stamina recovery when you are weighted down.
     Agility has effect on attack rates and your chance to be hit by
a monster. Shoes with good floor grip are useful here.
     Reason has a multiplier effect on how well a spell works. Also
it allows you to cast high level spells at a lower level. Note that
some spells may not be cast till sufficient level is reached.
     Vigor has a direct effect on your maximum health. Your maximum
health is equal to Vigor times your Level divided by two.
     In  the upper right you will see 4 vertical  bars. These  are
your status bars.  In all cases the higher the bars the better off 
you are. Starting from the left bar here is what they mean.
     The green bar is your current health. If this bar drops below 
zero then you will die.  The red  bar is your short  term  stamina
level  and affects your ability to complete actions.  If this  bar 
drops to low you will be unable to cast spells,  do melee attacks, 
and perform many other actions. This bar drops whenever you attack
or  perform many other actions.  The brown bar is your food  level 
and affects how fast you recover health.  The last or blue bar  is 
your water level and affects stamina recovery. Casting spells  and
using magic items can also cause dehydration.
     To open a door, click on it with the mouse. If there is a small
half circle at the top of the door, then the door is locked. To unlock
the door, hold the proper key in mouse pointer and click on the door
with it. The iron key unlocks any wood door.
     In a land far away a powerful wizard enchanted his life force
into a golden skull and proclaimed himself to be a god.  Then in a 
display  of his malevolence he conquered the citadel known as  the 
MYSTIC  MIRROR.  You play the part of adventurer who has vowed  to 
defeat  his evil plans and prevent the destruction of your  world.

HELPFUL HINTS:
1)  Get a character with good vigor. Health points are great  for
staying alive.

2)  Learn what to do with your treasure. Its not just  there  for
decoration.

3)  Watch  your food and water.  This affects  your  recovery  of
health and stamina. You should carry extra water.

4)  You will need to find keys to open certain doors.  There  are
four different keys you will probably need. If you accidently destroy
your keys, there is more than one way to open or get past most doors.

5)  Learn  the monsters weak spots.  Many monsters are immune  to
certain  attack forms.  It is quite difficult to kill the  walking 
dead with a death spell. 

6)  Many ordinary looking items actually have special powers.

7)  Some levels regenerate monsters. You can never clean them up.

8) The goal of the game is to kill the floating gold skull on the
top level. There are 10 levels in the game.

9) Don't miss the bag of holding early in game. This will save many
trips. Also objects in the bag of holding have no weight.

10) All the wells are slightly magical. You can slowly heal yourself
by drinking water from them.

